WEBVTT

00:41.175 --> 00:43.115
Ice cream is sweet, right?

00:43.115 --> 00:45.100
It's my favorite.

00:45.100 --> 00:48.693
Even the ice cream tastes sweeter today.

00:50.668 --> 00:53.299
But honestly... it still doesn't feel real.

00:53.299 --> 00:57.537
I like you, and you like me back.

00:57.537 --> 01:00.246
What are the odds of that?

01:00.246 --> 01:03.419
I know... it's kind of amazing.

01:04.313 --> 01:06.299
I think...

01:06.299 --> 01:10.345
I'm going to remember today for a long time.

01:10.345 --> 01:11.895
If we

01:11.895 --> 01:15.618
ever get upset or end up arguing,

01:15.618 --> 01:17.593
let's think back to today.

01:17.593 --> 01:20.780
Remember how we met against all odds

01:20.780 --> 01:23.011
and try to work through it.

01:23.011 --> 01:24.537
Yeah.

01:24.537 --> 01:26.250
But...

01:26.250 --> 01:29.770
I'll make sure it never comes to that.

01:34.939 --> 01:37.255
Want to walk a little longer?

01:37.255 --> 01:39.705
Just until we finish this?

01:39.705 --> 01:42.278
Sounds good.

01:47.792 --> 01:52.452
We should head back now.
At this rate, we'll be out all night.

01:52.452 --> 01:54.877
Feels like it's already getting light.

01:54.877 --> 01:56.561
Really?

01:56.561 --> 02:00.665
Time just flies when I'm with you.
Even the night feels too short.

02:00.665 --> 02:03.415
So... what are you doing tomorrow?

02:03.415 --> 02:06.269
Tomorrow? Nothing, really.

02:06.269 --> 02:09.722
I usually just rest and recharge on Sundays.

02:09.722 --> 02:11.933
Then how about doing that "nothing"

02:11.933 --> 02:14.386
together at my place tomorrow?

02:14.386 --> 02:17.852
- At your place?
- Yeah.

02:18.848 --> 02:19.885
Okay.

02:19.885 --> 02:22.610
I'll head over around lunchtime.

02:22.610 --> 02:23.875
Maybe... one?

02:23.875 --> 02:24.983
Come at twelve.

02:24.983 --> 02:27.556
- I'll cook something good.
- Oh, now I'm excited.

02:27.556 --> 02:30.250
Don't get your hopes up too much.

02:30.250 --> 02:32.943
You should go in.

02:47.996 --> 02:49.467
See you tomorrow... no,

02:49.467 --> 02:52.782
I'll see you really soon.

02:58.966 --> 03:02.085
This is unreal.

03:03.720 --> 03:09.757
[Episode 9]

03:17.242 --> 03:18.786
That night,

03:18.786 --> 03:23.446
I realized all over again...
love can be so cruel.

03:26.097 --> 03:28.828
Excuse me, could you pass this along?

03:28.828 --> 03:31.415
She lives here. Her name's Lee Ui Yeong.

03:31.415 --> 03:33.250
You're the one I saw before.

03:33.250 --> 03:36.735
Why not just give it to her yourself?

03:36.735 --> 03:38.521
I'd appreciate you taking care of it.

03:38.521 --> 03:39.548
Alright.

03:39.548 --> 03:43.102
It warms your heart to the point of burning...

03:43.102 --> 03:46.362
then suddenly turns ice-cold.

03:46.362 --> 03:49.592
It lets you feel
what it's like to be together...

03:49.592 --> 03:55.147
then suddenly makes you feel like
you could lose it all.

03:55.147 --> 03:56.440
[PT: 5 sessions for 300,000 won]

03:56.440 --> 03:58.984
I really wanted to make this work.

03:58.984 --> 04:00.412
[Time's up]

04:01.539 --> 04:03.016
Maybe that's why...

04:03.016 --> 04:07.593
the moment two hearts truly meet

04:07.593 --> 04:12.260
feels almost like a miracle.

04:12.260 --> 04:15.940
Love may keep playing tricks on us,

04:15.940 --> 04:20.106
but I won't lose to it.

04:20.106 --> 04:23.779
I should be a good man.

04:31.962 --> 04:35.242
When it comes to seasoning,
you stick with what you know.

04:35.242 --> 04:37.555
That's how it turns out good.

04:37.555 --> 04:40.521
- Oh, my son's calling.
- Yeah?

04:40.521 --> 04:42.853
- Hi, Mom.
- Hey, Tae Seop.

04:42.853 --> 04:45.297
I'm trying to make tteokbokki at home.

04:45.297 --> 04:46.703
How do you do the sauce?

04:46.703 --> 04:47.960
Tteokbokki?

04:47.960 --> 04:49.984
Oh, is Sua coming over?

04:49.984 --> 04:51.563
Then should I tell you a mild version?

04:51.563 --> 04:52.579
No.

04:52.579 --> 04:54.898
Like, adult-level spicy.

04:54.898 --> 04:56.697
Adult-level?

04:56.697 --> 04:59.022
Oh, wait...

04:59.022 --> 05:02.485
- Is this for that girl?
- Yeah.

05:02.485 --> 05:03.768
Actually...

05:03.768 --> 05:07.321
I'm seeing Ui Yeong now.

05:07.321 --> 05:10.318
He says they're seeing each other!

05:10.318 --> 05:13.602
Well then, I'll give you a bold, spicy recipe.

05:13.602 --> 05:17.103
You know how your dad fell for my cooking, huh?

05:17.103 --> 05:21.700
I tried to keep your mom out of the kitchen,
but her cooking was just too good.

05:21.700 --> 05:22.725
I know.

05:22.725 --> 05:24.903
Hope it works on me too.

05:24.903 --> 05:26.917
Of course it will.

05:26.917 --> 05:29.457
Now grab a pen. Gochujang, chili flakes,

05:29.457 --> 05:31.117
sugar, dashida,

05:31.117 --> 05:33.822
and don't forget minced garlic
and green onions.

05:33.822 --> 05:35.064
Add cooking oil too.

05:35.064 --> 05:36.305
Cooking oil too?

05:36.305 --> 05:38.458
Yeah, that's a pro tip.

05:38.458 --> 05:42.847
That's what brings all the flavors together.

05:42.847 --> 05:45.794
Then how much should I use?

05:47.121 --> 05:51.013
Okay, anything's possible.

05:51.827 --> 05:53.005
Well...

05:53.005 --> 05:55.472
At least the top and bottom should match.

05:55.472 --> 05:57.465
What looks better?

05:57.465 --> 05:59.439
Mom!

05:59.439 --> 06:03.438
Have you seen my light blue shirt?

06:03.438 --> 06:05.511
Yeah, that one.

06:05.511 --> 06:08.727
That's cold. What are you doing? My hair...

06:08.727 --> 06:10.949
Make me some ramen. Crack an egg in it.

06:10.949 --> 06:11.996
- Right now?
- Yeah.

06:11.996 --> 06:14.972
I've got lunch plans.
I'll at least get the water started.

06:14.972 --> 06:18.596
I'll make it for you tonight. Sorry.

06:18.596 --> 06:23.076
She's acting like
it's the morning of a field trip.

06:23.783 --> 06:26.336
Is she dating someone?

06:27.262 --> 06:28.300
Excuse me!

06:28.300 --> 06:30.960
- Oh, hello.
- Hello.

06:30.960 --> 06:33.957
A tall young guy dropped this off
late last night.

06:33.957 --> 06:35.691
It's yours, right?

06:35.691 --> 06:38.221
Yes, it is. Thank you.

06:38.221 --> 06:40.457
Let him know you got it, okay?

06:40.457 --> 06:42.998
I will.

06:51.375 --> 06:52.709
Ji Su,

06:52.709 --> 06:55.556
I got the cardigan. Thanks.

06:55.556 --> 06:58.976
Did you get home okay last night?

07:03.405 --> 07:05.909
Got the cardigan.

07:05.909 --> 07:08.902
Thanks.

07:43.955 --> 07:46.026
Congrats.

07:46.026 --> 07:48.319
On officially being in a relationship.

07:48.319 --> 07:51.885
Thanks. I'll take it.

07:58.370 --> 08:02.700
That smells so good. Looks amazing.

08:05.032 --> 08:09.442
Add the green onions... and fish cake.

08:09.442 --> 08:11.695
So this is how you do it.

08:11.695 --> 08:14.962
Tteokbokki really is different in every house.

08:14.962 --> 08:16.946
Then how is it at your place?

08:16.946 --> 08:18.639
Well...

08:18.639 --> 08:21.163
No style is kind of our style.

08:21.163 --> 08:22.738
What?

08:22.738 --> 08:26.409
My mom was always busy,
so we mostly bought food from outside.

08:26.409 --> 08:30.842
Even kimchi stew and stuff,
we never really had a right way.

08:30.842 --> 08:34.436
- Can you just add all the fish cake?
- Sure.

08:34.436 --> 08:36.986
- You really like fish cake, huh?
- It looks so good.

08:36.986 --> 08:38.463
Here.

08:38.463 --> 08:40.630
- Try it while it's hot.
- Okay.

08:40.630 --> 08:43.430
I'll try the rice cake first.

08:46.961 --> 08:48.898
How is it?

08:48.898 --> 08:50.108
- It's so good.
- Really?

08:50.108 --> 08:51.881
Yeah!

08:51.881 --> 08:54.888
That's a relief.

08:54.888 --> 08:57.754
I need to try the fish cake too.

09:12.391 --> 09:16.848
You were so fair and tiny.

09:16.848 --> 09:20.143
How does someone this small end up this tall?

09:20.143 --> 09:21.770
I think it was around junior year
in high school.

09:21.770 --> 09:24.242
I just shot up out of nowhere.

09:24.242 --> 09:27.242
Oh, your parents.

09:29.867 --> 09:34.819
Are there no photos after you started school?

09:34.819 --> 09:37.376
My dad's company went under,

09:37.376 --> 09:42.029
and that's when my parents opened
their restaurant together.

09:42.695 --> 09:46.206
Around the time you said
the dining table was gone?

09:46.206 --> 09:48.292
Yeah.

09:51.132 --> 09:52.263
Here it is.

09:52.263 --> 09:54.607
My dad had a real knack for business.

09:54.607 --> 09:56.747
Everyone was struggling back then,

09:56.747 --> 09:59.577
so he figured selling spicy chicken feet
near office areas

09:59.577 --> 10:02.084
would at least keep them afloat.

10:02.084 --> 10:05.251
He trusted my mom's cooking and went for it.

10:05.251 --> 10:09.007
Starting a business for the first time,
and a chicken feet place on top of that...

10:09.007 --> 10:10.644
it must've been really tough.

10:10.644 --> 10:12.023
Yeah. When things got hard,

10:12.023 --> 10:17.237
they just leaned on each other
and got through it.

10:17.237 --> 10:19.081
I think I get it now.

10:19.081 --> 10:23.394
Why you see marriage as something so natural.

10:24.346 --> 10:26.983
I've never really said this before...

10:26.983 --> 10:28.176
Yeah?

10:28.176 --> 10:32.620
My parents have been separated for a long time.

10:32.620 --> 10:35.044
Oh, I see.

10:35.044 --> 10:39.350
They're just too different. Total opposites.

10:39.350 --> 10:41.908
So I guess for me,

10:41.908 --> 10:45.608
marriage always feels like
someone else's story.

10:45.608 --> 10:49.686
Maybe that's why dating feels harder too.

10:49.686 --> 10:51.855
Like... with tteokbokki or kimchi stew,

10:51.855 --> 10:54.650
I don't really have a right way.

10:55.817 --> 10:57.414
But that's okay.

10:57.414 --> 10:58.444
Like earlier,

10:58.444 --> 11:01.322
you can add more fish cake,
put in what you like.

11:01.322 --> 11:03.241
That works too.

11:03.241 --> 11:06.407
We can just... do love our own way.

11:06.407 --> 11:09.013
I like that.

11:09.013 --> 11:10.244
Then...

11:10.244 --> 11:13.197
How about this?

11:14.197 --> 11:15.894
This one.

11:15.894 --> 11:17.380
Can I have this photo?

11:17.380 --> 11:20.299
That one's a rare level of cute, though.

11:20.299 --> 11:22.119
What?

11:22.772 --> 11:24.523
You've got tons of cute ones.

11:24.523 --> 11:27.560
Then bring one of yours.

11:27.560 --> 11:28.753
Let's trade.

11:28.753 --> 11:30.811
- This level of cute?
- It has to be that level.

11:30.811 --> 11:33.172
Do I even have one? That's a tough ask.

11:33.172 --> 11:34.694
[Deukgeun Deukgeun Gym]

11:36.341 --> 11:38.445
- Hold on a second.
- Sure.

11:38.445 --> 11:41.325
Hello? Hey, I'm...

11:41.967 --> 11:44.038
Lee Ui Yeong.

11:44.038 --> 11:46.412
Are you crying?

11:46.412 --> 11:49.108
Can you come right now?

11:49.108 --> 11:51.421
Right now?

11:54.507 --> 11:57.238
I really

11:57.238 --> 12:00.384
meant it with her.

12:07.195 --> 12:09.891
And I think she did too.

12:09.891 --> 12:12.309
She got her hands all greasy

12:12.309 --> 12:15.762
pulling chicken apart just to feed me...

12:22.762 --> 12:26.848
I'm such an idiot.

12:26.848 --> 12:29.514
I'm pathetic.

12:31.228 --> 12:35.175
Such a coward...

12:36.778 --> 12:38.294
Lim Seung Jun.

12:38.294 --> 12:41.757
Yeah, that's me.

12:43.376 --> 12:45.051
How much did you drink?

12:45.051 --> 12:47.321
Who's this?

12:47.321 --> 12:49.072
My boyfriend.

12:49.072 --> 12:51.012
He was with me when I picked up, so...

12:51.012 --> 12:52.058
Say hi.

12:52.058 --> 12:54.268
Hello, I'm Song Tae Seop.

12:54.268 --> 12:58.551
- Say hi.
- Your boyfriend?

12:58.551 --> 13:00.621
Oh, okay.

13:00.621 --> 13:02.986
Hello. I'm Lim Seung Jun.

13:02.986 --> 13:05.974
Nice to meet you.

13:05.974 --> 13:10.514
Ui Yeong is finally dating.

13:10.514 --> 13:14.207
Even Ui Yeong has a boyfriend...

13:17.047 --> 13:20.148
and me...

13:20.148 --> 13:23.027
I'm just...

13:24.187 --> 13:27.673
Hey, what are you doing?

13:27.673 --> 13:30.781
Come on, let's get you out of here.

13:30.781 --> 13:34.600
I've got him. Here, let's get you up.

13:34.600 --> 13:36.561
Be careful.

13:36.561 --> 13:38.453
I'm so sorry.

13:38.453 --> 13:40.446
Seriously...

13:43.565 --> 13:45.704
Oh my.

13:47.966 --> 13:50.675
Oh my gosh.

13:52.095 --> 13:53.487
Are you okay?

13:53.487 --> 13:56.620
How much did you even drink?

13:56.620 --> 13:59.960
- Big guy, zero tolerance.
- Let's get you lying down.

14:02.211 --> 14:06.049
- Beats me.
- Have some of this.

14:08.147 --> 14:11.053
You're so kind.

14:11.053 --> 14:13.524
But her?

14:13.524 --> 14:16.121
She needs more than just "kind."

14:16.121 --> 14:20.228
She's kind of high maintenance, honestly.

14:20.228 --> 14:23.013
Yeah? Must be cute.

14:23.013 --> 14:26.389
But you're kind of a handful yourself today.

14:26.389 --> 14:27.486
I'm sorry.

14:27.486 --> 14:30.399
Hey, you should've told me sooner.

14:30.399 --> 14:32.423
Why'd you let it get this bad?

14:32.423 --> 14:35.419
You were too busy talking about yourself.

14:35.419 --> 14:39.326
Did you even care how I was doing?

14:39.326 --> 14:40.565
Come on,

14:40.565 --> 14:43.244
you can't just say apps are casual
and blind dates are serious.

14:43.244 --> 14:46.013
That's not how it works.
You know, I'm living proof.

14:46.013 --> 14:48.605
Do you know how many weird people show up
on blind dates?

14:48.605 --> 14:51.636
Want me to list them all?

14:51.636 --> 14:55.599
You've been on quite a few blind dates, huh?

14:56.349 --> 14:58.976
Hey, just tell her you had some biases.

14:58.976 --> 15:03.411
Say you didn't really know,
and you were wrong to brush it off like that.

15:03.411 --> 15:05.009
Just say you were nervous.

15:05.009 --> 15:07.527
I can't. I can't say that.

15:07.527 --> 15:09.889
Why not?

15:09.889 --> 15:12.620
- I already got blocked.
- Blocked you?

15:12.620 --> 15:14.867
Seriously, she went that far?

15:14.867 --> 15:15.896
Hey, forget it.

15:15.896 --> 15:17.825
You shouldn't be with someone like that.

15:17.825 --> 15:21.163
You'd just be on edge the whole time.

15:21.163 --> 15:24.062
Just let it go, okay? Forget her.

15:24.062 --> 15:25.920
You hear me?

15:25.920 --> 15:28.962
Hey, say something!

15:30.140 --> 15:33.300
Come on, why are you crying?

15:46.155 --> 15:48.822
No one can control him.

15:50.869 --> 15:54.046
He used to play basketball back in the day.

15:54.046 --> 15:57.286
Then he got seriously injured.

15:57.286 --> 16:00.620
So even getting into his line of work was
really hard for him.

16:00.620 --> 16:03.244
He looks tough on the outside,

16:03.244 --> 16:06.242
but I know how soft he really is.

16:06.242 --> 16:11.115
I just want him to take the easy road for once.

16:11.774 --> 16:14.018
But when things get hard,

16:14.018 --> 16:16.745
you'll be there for him, right?

16:16.745 --> 16:19.218
Of course.

16:19.218 --> 16:23.136
And...
sorry you had to deal with all that today.

16:23.136 --> 16:27.064
I got to make tteokbokki, meet your friend...

16:27.064 --> 16:29.363
and I feel like we got closer today.

16:29.363 --> 16:31.613
I like that.

16:31.613 --> 16:33.029
Me too.

16:33.029 --> 16:36.237
Honestly, a home date like this
beats most hotel stays.

16:36.237 --> 16:38.341
You like hotel stays?

16:38.341 --> 16:41.852
Yeah.
And I like checking out different hotels too.

16:41.852 --> 16:42.914
I see.

16:42.914 --> 16:45.959
Then next time, maybe we...

16:47.228 --> 16:49.086
Let's go together next time.

16:49.086 --> 16:51.756
Whenever you want.

16:51.756 --> 16:53.926
I'd like that.

16:54.861 --> 16:58.327
So how's work these days? Busy?

16:58.327 --> 17:02.881
Yeah, I'll be pretty busy for a while
because of the exhibition.

17:02.881 --> 17:06.026
- Then our next date...
- Saturday.

17:06.026 --> 17:07.063
Saturday?

17:07.063 --> 17:09.372
If we meet on Saturday, we can stay out late.

17:09.372 --> 17:12.732
Oh, that makes sense.

17:13.953 --> 17:16.319
I can't wait.

17:20.131 --> 17:21.995
Have a good one.

17:21.995 --> 17:24.795
Hang in there this Monday.

17:31.839 --> 17:34.919
Why are they renewing
a perfectly fine gift set?

17:34.919 --> 17:37.176
We go out every year, visit the farms,
manage all the vendors...

17:37.176 --> 17:39.442
and this is how they treat us?

17:39.442 --> 17:42.448
You don't think it's a quality issue, do you?

17:42.448 --> 17:43.474
No way.

17:43.474 --> 17:46.018
You know how strict we are with inspections.

17:46.018 --> 17:47.052
Whatever.

17:47.052 --> 17:48.562
The team manager will deal with it.

17:48.562 --> 17:52.317
He hates anything that's a hassle anyway.

17:54.624 --> 17:58.051
The meeting hasn't even started,
and you're already exhausted?

17:58.051 --> 18:00.184
Sorry?

18:01.541 --> 18:03.489
I had something come up.

18:03.489 --> 18:07.206
What happened? Oh, right.

18:07.206 --> 18:09.668
Want this?

18:11.460 --> 18:14.338
Isn't this what I gave you last time?

18:14.338 --> 18:17.758
Yeah. I had this and
it got me through the whole day.

18:17.758 --> 18:20.846
- You need the energy.
- You're an angel.

18:21.470 --> 18:23.389
What is it? I want one too.

18:23.389 --> 18:25.057
Here, you should have one too.

18:25.057 --> 18:28.143
I'm already exhausted.

18:28.143 --> 18:29.812
Alright, let's go.

18:29.812 --> 18:32.941
Okay, let's do this.

18:36.432 --> 18:37.465
Let's go.

18:37.465 --> 18:42.013
Grocery platforms are carrying
premium ingredients now,

18:42.013 --> 18:44.270
so our gift sets aren't as competitive
as they used to be.

18:44.270 --> 18:46.950
I think it's time we refresh the lineup.

18:46.950 --> 18:49.674
Food trends really move fast these days.

18:49.674 --> 18:51.334
Just look at social media.

18:51.334 --> 18:53.558
Pasta one week, tteokbokki the next.

18:53.558 --> 18:55.622
- The trending recipes keep changing.
- Exactly.

18:55.622 --> 18:59.759
But do we really need to chase every trend?

18:59.759 --> 19:03.222
We're a hotel, after all.

19:06.187 --> 19:08.131
Don't you think, sir?

19:08.131 --> 19:10.384
Yeah, that's true.

19:10.384 --> 19:12.897
We can't just follow everything.

19:12.897 --> 19:17.985
But if sales are down,
we need to do something, right?

19:17.985 --> 19:22.531
This might be something for
marketing to handle.

19:22.531 --> 19:25.662
I've actually been thinking about that.

19:25.662 --> 19:28.741
Have you heard of the Ark of Flavor project?

19:28.741 --> 19:30.209
- Ark?
- Ark of Flavor?

19:30.209 --> 19:31.749
No, I haven't.

19:31.749 --> 19:34.694
It's about preserving food diversity,

19:34.694 --> 19:38.222
and there are
quite a few registered items in Korea.

19:38.222 --> 19:41.495
- You came prepared.
- Oh, okay.

19:41.495 --> 19:44.822
Alright, let's take a look.

19:46.721 --> 19:47.744
[Ark of Flavor]

19:47.744 --> 19:50.439
It aligns with the hotel's values,

19:50.439 --> 19:53.979
and I think it'll appeal to customers
who want their purchases to mean something.

19:53.979 --> 19:58.317
This is seriously advanced.

19:58.317 --> 20:00.315
We'll be traveling
all over the country for this.

20:00.315 --> 20:02.238
It's a tough one,

20:02.238 --> 20:05.345
but if we pull it off,
it'll really prove what we can do.

20:05.345 --> 20:07.454
Right?

20:30.226 --> 20:33.060
The director has high expectations.

20:33.060 --> 20:37.442
He buys these sets every year
to give out as gifts.

20:37.442 --> 20:39.097
This is our chance.

20:39.097 --> 20:41.569
Let's do a good job and score some points.

20:41.569 --> 20:44.781
- Absolutely.
- Alright, let's get to it.

20:47.137 --> 20:49.326
How are we going to source the vendors?

20:49.326 --> 20:52.941
I'll start by listing what we can get
through our current partners.

20:52.941 --> 20:54.753
Then I'll start making calls.

20:54.753 --> 20:56.208
And for anything else,

20:56.208 --> 20:59.860
we'll probably have to go out
and find it ourselves.

20:59.860 --> 21:01.850
I'll hit the markets with you.

21:01.850 --> 21:02.882
Okay.

21:02.882 --> 21:06.115
- Let's all hang in there.
- Yeah.

21:06.115 --> 21:08.083
[Have a good one]

21:13.793 --> 21:15.430
Are you really that happy?

21:15.430 --> 21:18.954
Reading into emojis like that?
Even Sua doesn't do that.

21:18.954 --> 21:21.791
Why wouldn't I be? It's a heart.

21:21.791 --> 21:25.308
A star could mean anything,

21:25.308 --> 21:28.741
but a heart's just a heart.

21:28.741 --> 21:31.505
Man, I'm jealous.

21:31.505 --> 21:35.362
As your friend, I'm really happy for you two.

21:35.362 --> 21:37.773
But as your business partner,

21:37.773 --> 21:41.629
before I toss your phone,
pick the pieces for the exhibition first.

21:41.629 --> 21:44.842
I was about to.

21:48.469 --> 21:50.930
[Tuning the Everyday - Exhibition Proposal]

21:50.930 --> 21:53.807
[Concept: Connecting each designer's philosophy
to living objects]

21:53.807 --> 21:55.518
What's there to overthink?

21:55.518 --> 21:56.936
They're basically telling you
to do whatever you want.

21:56.936 --> 22:00.649
That's exactly why it's harder.
There's no client.

22:01.321 --> 22:03.921
Okay.

22:03.921 --> 22:06.760
We're at the corner.

22:08.908 --> 22:12.034
- What's going on?
- No idea.

22:12.034 --> 22:16.572
Alright, you can put your hands down
and open your eyes.

22:18.675 --> 22:23.837
Wait, is this my chair? Seriously?

22:23.837 --> 22:27.091
- You can even put your name on it.
- We'll send it to your place.

22:27.091 --> 22:29.755
The seat stays comfortable even for long hours,

22:29.755 --> 22:31.941
and the backrest supports you nicely.

22:31.941 --> 22:35.285
Go on, try it. You won't know until you sit.

22:37.822 --> 22:43.873
Wow, it's so soft. This is amazing.

22:43.873 --> 22:47.736
I think this might be the best gift
I've ever gotten.

22:47.736 --> 22:49.040
Really?

22:49.040 --> 22:51.403
The gift-givers look more excited.

22:51.403 --> 22:53.365
That's how gifts work.

22:53.365 --> 22:56.084
Oh, you wouldn't know.

22:56.084 --> 22:58.080
You're always making stuff on commission,

22:58.080 --> 23:01.241
and if something doesn't turn out right,
you just take it home.

23:01.241 --> 23:06.494
You've never made something
just to give it as a gift, have you?

23:08.181 --> 23:10.602
You're right. I haven't.

23:10.602 --> 23:13.839
I guess I don't really get that feeling.

23:13.839 --> 23:16.903
Then take this chance and make me something...

23:16.903 --> 23:18.348
No.

23:18.348 --> 23:19.409
Okay, bye.

23:19.409 --> 23:21.437
[The artists' deeply personal works]
Is it comfortable?

23:21.437 --> 23:22.981
[connect with the audience's emotions]

23:26.108 --> 23:28.242
Glad you figured it out.

23:28.242 --> 23:30.112
So what are you making?

23:30.112 --> 23:31.488
You'll see.

23:31.488 --> 23:34.552
I think I'll get the chance to show you.

23:34.552 --> 23:36.422
So you're heading out after dinner?

23:36.422 --> 23:37.453
Yes.

23:37.453 --> 23:40.506
Hyun Min's been kind of down all day,

23:40.506 --> 23:42.275
so I'm taking her out for something good.

23:42.275 --> 23:44.575
Make sure you eat too.

23:44.575 --> 23:47.247
Alright. Enjoy your dinner.

23:47.247 --> 23:48.297
Thanks.

23:48.297 --> 23:51.495
[A Chair for Lovers]
[Kind, delicate]

23:51.495 --> 23:54.004
[Honest]

23:59.673 --> 24:02.027
Hyun Min, I'm sorry.

24:02.027 --> 24:04.065
Dinner's on me tonight,
so eat as much as you want.

24:04.065 --> 24:05.105
- Really?
- Yeah.

24:05.105 --> 24:06.809
- Then I'm ordering drinks too.
- Go for it.

24:06.809 --> 24:10.540
Excuse me, we'll have
a large bottle of gaoliang.

24:10.540 --> 24:11.570
Sure.

24:11.570 --> 24:14.274
But why were you in the restroom so long?

24:14.274 --> 24:15.741
Everything okay?

24:15.741 --> 24:19.457
Well, I was just on the phone.

24:19.457 --> 24:21.574
With Tae Seop.

24:21.574 --> 24:26.227
Work's done, so what were you talking about?

24:30.129 --> 24:34.339
Actually, I'm... seeing Tae Seop now.

24:34.339 --> 24:35.889
Since that farewell party.

24:35.889 --> 24:39.390
- No way! You met him that night?
- Yeah.

24:39.390 --> 24:42.419
I got there really late
and wasn't sure he'd still be there,

24:42.419 --> 24:43.894
but he was waiting.

24:43.894 --> 24:47.572
Nodding off the whole time. Isn't he cute?

24:47.572 --> 24:49.129
"Cute?"

24:49.129 --> 24:53.679
Well... as long as he makes you happy,
that's all that matters.

24:53.679 --> 24:56.573
Congrats, Ui Yeong.

24:56.573 --> 24:57.991
Thanks.

24:57.991 --> 25:00.452
So that long marathon of blind dates
is finally over.

25:00.452 --> 25:02.656
I know.

25:02.656 --> 25:06.162
- Congrats!
- The food's here.

25:06.162 --> 25:07.334
Thank you.

25:07.334 --> 25:09.253
Guess we're having a celebratory drink tonight.

25:09.253 --> 25:11.653
Yeah!

25:11.653 --> 25:14.213
Thank you.

25:21.485 --> 25:24.071
I'm so full.

25:30.654 --> 25:32.230
But

25:32.230 --> 25:35.074
how does that even work?

25:35.074 --> 25:36.500
What?

25:36.500 --> 25:41.373
Like, a relationship built on trust.

25:41.373 --> 25:43.260
Trust?

25:43.260 --> 25:47.521
That's just something that builds naturally
as you spend time together.

25:47.521 --> 25:49.005
I mean...

25:49.005 --> 25:50.710
People say

25:50.710 --> 25:53.265
there's someone you marry,
and someone you just date for fun.

25:53.265 --> 25:55.841
The person you marry

25:55.841 --> 25:59.094
and the person you date can be different.

25:59.094 --> 26:01.576
Come on, that's just something people say.

26:01.576 --> 26:06.762
How do you divide people like that
before you even get to know them?

26:07.762 --> 26:09.285
I think people do.

26:09.285 --> 26:11.231
What? Did someone say something to you?

26:11.231 --> 26:13.694
Who was it?

26:15.822 --> 26:19.406
I met a guy recently through an app.

26:19.406 --> 26:21.497
- A dating app?
- No!

26:21.497 --> 26:24.510
Not a dating app...

26:25.768 --> 26:27.873
Soonmu Market.

26:27.873 --> 26:30.669
Soonmu.

26:33.171 --> 26:34.481
Really?

26:34.481 --> 26:38.494
People actually meet like that these days?

26:39.357 --> 26:43.764
Excuse me! Another bottle of gaoliang, please!

26:43.764 --> 26:46.810
- Sure.
- Hurry.

26:49.444 --> 26:51.624
Are you okay?

26:54.817 --> 26:57.088
Did you finish?

26:57.088 --> 26:58.557
Yeah.

26:58.557 --> 27:01.156
Are you feeling that bad?

27:01.156 --> 27:03.021
I shouldn't have let you drink so much.

27:03.021 --> 27:05.507
Come on, lie down.

27:07.975 --> 27:10.241
Beats me.

27:11.342 --> 27:15.032
Hey, I know you pretty well, right?

27:15.032 --> 27:18.076
You might be a little eccentric,

27:18.076 --> 27:20.968
but you're not the kind of person
to screw someone over.

27:20.968 --> 27:22.719
If a guy can't see that, he's not worth it.

27:22.719 --> 27:24.290
Just let him go. Okay?

27:24.290 --> 27:26.932
He's already gone.

27:26.932 --> 27:29.340
I'm taking the day off tomorrow.

27:29.340 --> 27:32.110
Okay, just get some rest.

27:32.110 --> 27:34.347
I'll leave you water
and something for the hangover.

27:34.347 --> 27:36.960
Make sure you take it, alright?

27:53.972 --> 27:57.281
She really went overboard.

28:27.131 --> 28:29.234
I'm such an idiot. I'm pathetic.

28:29.234 --> 28:31.163
- Such a coward...
- The person you marry

28:31.163 --> 28:35.011
and the person you date can be different.

28:35.011 --> 28:37.256
I bought it used to read over the weekend.

28:37.256 --> 28:40.019
I met someone through a resale app...

28:40.019 --> 28:41.908
Forget it.
You shouldn't be with someone like that.

28:41.908 --> 28:43.926
You'd just be on edge the whole time.

28:43.926 --> 28:45.699
I met a guy recently through an app.

28:45.699 --> 28:48.068
Soonmu Market...

28:48.068 --> 28:50.390
Someone I met through resale...

28:50.390 --> 28:53.213
No way.

28:53.213 --> 28:57.438
[Deukgeun Deukgeun Gym]

28:58.286 --> 29:00.638
I'm home.

29:02.972 --> 29:05.345
Mom.

29:06.465 --> 29:08.867
- Why does the world feel so small?
- Why?

29:08.867 --> 29:12.412
My friend and my coworker...

29:12.412 --> 29:13.652
I think they've got something going on.

29:13.652 --> 29:15.687
Who, Seung Jun?

29:15.687 --> 29:17.663
You didn't set them up, did you?

29:17.663 --> 29:19.705
No.

29:19.705 --> 29:23.442
I feel like I might've messed things up.

29:23.442 --> 29:25.815
Come on.

29:25.815 --> 29:29.405
You're still a third party,
no matter how close you are to them.

29:29.405 --> 29:31.936
Don't get involved.

29:31.936 --> 29:36.776
And maybe they just didn't tell you
because it wasn't your place to know.

29:38.232 --> 29:39.272
Yeah.

29:39.272 --> 29:40.902
It's between them.

29:40.902 --> 29:44.775
And it's not something I can fix anyway.

29:50.987 --> 29:53.078
We've got everything else sorted,

29:53.078 --> 29:54.991
so now we just need to find Chikso.

29:54.991 --> 29:56.035
Alright, let's do it.

29:56.035 --> 29:57.082
In a market this big,

29:57.082 --> 29:59.837
there's got to be at least one vendor
who knows a farm, huh?

29:59.837 --> 30:01.129
- Then let's start...
- Where?

30:01.129 --> 30:04.977
- Let's just go one by one from here.
- Okay, okay.

30:04.977 --> 30:07.300
- Hello.
- Hi.

30:07.300 --> 30:08.938
Do you carry Chikso?

30:08.938 --> 30:10.887
- No, we don't.
- Do you know anywhere that does?

30:10.887 --> 30:13.642
You probably won't find it around here.

30:14.401 --> 30:16.486
- Hello, sir.
- Welcome.

30:16.486 --> 30:18.895
Do you happen to carry Chikso?

30:18.895 --> 30:20.820
No, we don't deal with Chikso.

30:20.820 --> 30:24.703
- I see. Thank you.
- Have a good day.

30:27.020 --> 30:28.613
- Hello, sir.
- Hi.

30:28.613 --> 30:30.323
Do you know any Chikso farms?

30:30.323 --> 30:31.450
No, I don't.

30:31.450 --> 30:34.991
Oh, okay. Thank you.

30:34.991 --> 30:36.335
No.

30:36.335 --> 30:40.985
- We don't carry that.
- Got it, thank you.

30:43.339 --> 30:44.979
- Did you find anything?
- No.

30:44.979 --> 30:47.007
Same here. I'll keep checking the rest.

30:47.007 --> 30:50.387
- Then I'll take this side.
- I'll call you.

30:53.533 --> 30:55.515
We don't carry it.

30:55.515 --> 30:58.295
Alright, thank you.

31:00.634 --> 31:02.658
I think we've checked almost everywhere.

31:02.658 --> 31:04.978
Yeah, looks like no one has it.

31:04.978 --> 31:07.743
Wait, it says there's a butcher shop over here.

31:07.743 --> 31:10.178
Really? I think I saw a herbal shop earlier.

31:10.178 --> 31:14.055
It's almost closing time,
so I'll stop by Mr. Shin's place real quick.

31:14.055 --> 31:17.701
- Call me as soon as you find anything.
- Will do.

31:24.628 --> 31:27.851
[Oreum Butcher Shop]

31:30.886 --> 31:34.976
[Boiled Meat Specialty Shop]

31:39.036 --> 31:43.887
Hello, sir. I'm from The Hills Hotel.

31:43.887 --> 31:46.441
- What can I get you?
- I'm not buying anything.

31:46.441 --> 31:52.145
I was wondering if you might know
any Chikso farms.

31:52.145 --> 31:55.175
Chikso? Well...

31:55.175 --> 31:59.160
Was it Mr. Choi who raises Chikso?
Or was it black cattle?

31:59.160 --> 32:02.136
Oh, you know someone? Where?

32:02.136 --> 32:06.896
Somewhere... Gangwon-do or Gyeongsang-do.

32:08.190 --> 32:10.268
I can't remember all of a sudden.

32:10.268 --> 32:12.884
Maybe it's because business is so slow today.

32:12.884 --> 32:15.848
Oh, right.

32:17.068 --> 32:20.971
I'll take some Hanwoo to grill.

32:20.971 --> 32:26.998
Two of your best cuts, please.

32:29.241 --> 32:32.614
Not sure if I'll remember.

32:37.887 --> 32:40.377
Here you go, two nice cuts of sirloin...

32:40.377 --> 32:42.038
and here's the number.

32:42.038 --> 32:44.166
[Choi Sang Woo]
Thank you so much, sir.

32:44.166 --> 32:47.452
- You're a lifesaver.
- My pleasure.

32:47.452 --> 32:51.676
But that Mr. Choi... he's pretty stubborn.

32:51.676 --> 32:55.639
Not sure how he'll get along with you ladies.

32:59.841 --> 33:03.461
What, are you worried about what he said?

33:03.461 --> 33:08.011
There's a lot to work out,
so who he is matters too.

33:08.011 --> 33:09.421
True.

33:09.421 --> 33:12.652
Someone raising something that rare
isn't exactly easygoing.

33:12.652 --> 33:16.829
They've got the upper hand here,
so we'll just have to go along with it.

33:16.829 --> 33:19.275
Yeah, I know.

33:19.275 --> 33:21.552
Don't worry about it.

33:21.552 --> 33:26.661
I'll set up the meeting
and handle all the communication.

33:26.661 --> 33:29.521
Okay.

33:29.521 --> 33:33.275
You seem really upbeat these days.

33:33.275 --> 33:35.367
- Me?
- Yeah.

33:36.218 --> 33:40.891
I don't know,
I've just been motivated at work lately.

33:41.508 --> 33:44.611
But we still have to go wrap things up,

33:44.611 --> 33:46.802
so let's grab some coffee on the way.

33:46.802 --> 33:50.627
- Oh, I'm good.
- Don't worry, it's on me.

33:50.627 --> 33:53.307
- No, it's just...
- Come on.

33:55.214 --> 33:58.487
We need coffee.

34:01.601 --> 34:04.166
Alright, I'll go with...

34:04.166 --> 34:05.914
- Could you put the points on this?
- Okay.

34:05.914 --> 34:08.168
Hold on.

34:09.151 --> 34:11.288
Hey, I need to take this.

34:11.288 --> 34:15.534
I'll have something hot. No, iced one.

34:16.219 --> 34:17.759
Hello?

34:17.759 --> 34:20.053
Two iced Americanos to go.

34:20.053 --> 34:22.266
Okay.

34:23.406 --> 34:25.029
Here.

34:25.029 --> 34:27.468
Thanks.

34:29.046 --> 34:30.468
How have you been?

34:30.468 --> 34:33.429
Did you get home okay that night?

34:33.429 --> 34:36.462
That was forever ago. Why are you asking now?

34:36.462 --> 34:39.415
What do you think?

34:42.040 --> 34:43.623
Sorry.

34:43.623 --> 34:44.995
Don't be.

34:44.995 --> 34:48.790
You just followed your heart.

34:48.790 --> 34:51.571
I've been so busy lately,
I haven't even had time to feel anything.

34:51.571 --> 34:54.081
What about that audition you mentioned?

34:54.081 --> 34:55.485
Are you doing it?

34:55.485 --> 35:00.413
- Yeah, I think I am.
- That's amazing.

35:00.413 --> 35:04.503
What about you? Are you seeing Tae Seop?

35:05.847 --> 35:09.373
Yeah, we decided to give it a shot.

35:10.944 --> 35:13.254
So that's why you stopped coming by the cafe?

35:13.254 --> 35:15.652
Did he tell you not to come?

35:15.652 --> 35:19.058
Or are you trying to help me move on?

35:19.908 --> 35:21.865
Nothing's really changed.

35:21.865 --> 35:25.704
We're just back to being friends.

35:27.031 --> 35:29.033
It's not like we dated and broke up.

35:29.033 --> 35:32.455
What is this, the Stone Age?

35:33.877 --> 35:37.692
Fine. I'll keep my distance

35:37.692 --> 35:39.674
and not make things awkward.

35:39.674 --> 35:41.970
Yeah?

35:44.314 --> 35:47.474
Okay, I get it.

35:49.290 --> 35:53.170
- Is the coffee ready? Let's go.
- Yeah.

35:53.170 --> 35:55.996
- I'll see you again.
- Okay.

36:02.496 --> 36:07.766
So we've decided to cast you in the role.

36:07.766 --> 36:10.733
Mr. Shin Ji Su?

36:10.733 --> 36:14.306
I really appreciate the opportunity.

36:17.738 --> 36:20.042
Welcome.

36:20.042 --> 36:22.066
Oh, Ji Su is here.

36:22.066 --> 36:26.107
Was this supposed to be a surprise?
I'm not a fan of surprises.

36:26.107 --> 36:31.246
Sorry for the surprise. Please, have a seat.

36:45.739 --> 36:49.826
You don't really talk about
acting with your mom, right?

36:49.826 --> 36:51.495
Why not?

36:53.326 --> 36:54.499
That's not exactly common.

36:54.499 --> 36:58.046
Do you discuss directing with your mother?

36:59.131 --> 37:02.122
When you put it that way, I guess not.

37:02.122 --> 37:04.146
I've built my career on my own,

37:04.146 --> 37:06.170
and I plan to keep it that way.

37:06.170 --> 37:08.620
We're not related by blood,

37:08.620 --> 37:10.917
but we're a lot alike personality-wise.

37:10.917 --> 37:12.142
Director,

37:12.142 --> 37:14.686
you didn't cast him just because

37:14.686 --> 37:16.885
I mentioned I was reviewing
your next project, did you?

37:16.885 --> 37:19.561
No, of course not.

37:19.561 --> 37:22.351
He was simply the best fit for the role.

37:22.351 --> 37:24.112
Then this meeting should've been separate.

37:24.112 --> 37:28.001
It's too easy to misunderstand.
And this is his first drama.

37:28.001 --> 37:31.374
Wouldn't he want
more direct communication with you?

37:31.374 --> 37:33.711
You really don't understand actors.

37:33.711 --> 37:35.591
Oh, I see.

37:35.591 --> 37:39.344
Feel free to request time like that anytime.

37:39.344 --> 37:42.551
Okay, thank you.

37:47.156 --> 37:49.180
I was going to treat you. What a shame.

37:49.180 --> 37:51.055
Please give the script a good read.

37:51.055 --> 37:53.792
If it's good, I'll enjoy it.

37:53.792 --> 37:56.978
Your car's here. You should go.
I need a word with Ji Su.

37:56.978 --> 37:59.413
Alright then.

37:59.413 --> 38:02.233
- See you on set.
- Yeah.

38:02.233 --> 38:04.706
Have a safe trip.

38:07.863 --> 38:12.007
I'll try to shut down
situations like this when I can,

38:12.007 --> 38:14.971
but as long as you're in this industry,
you can't avoid them completely.

38:14.971 --> 38:17.642
- I know what I'm getting into.
- Then next time,

38:17.642 --> 38:19.542
use it to your advantage.

38:19.542 --> 38:21.363
You handled yourself well today.

38:21.363 --> 38:25.401
So did you.

38:25.401 --> 38:26.938
It was nothing.

38:26.938 --> 38:28.524
Anyway, congrats on the drama.

38:28.524 --> 38:33.175
I'll keep up with you on TV. I'm heading out.

38:49.781 --> 38:51.807
Did you get some rest?

38:51.807 --> 38:55.004
Yeah. I feel a lot better.

38:55.004 --> 38:58.074
I realized I can't let a guy
make me regret my life.

38:58.074 --> 39:01.504
I even put the comics back up
on Soonmu Market.

39:01.504 --> 39:04.534
So you really decided to move on?

39:04.534 --> 39:08.398
It's not like I didn't try.

39:08.398 --> 39:13.011
I even blocked him
so I wouldn't drunk-text him.

39:14.056 --> 39:17.800
So you blocked him to stop yourself
from texting him first?

39:17.800 --> 39:18.873
Yeah...

39:18.873 --> 39:22.890
I got my hopes up, and when he didn't text,
it just sucked.

39:22.890 --> 39:25.523
Yeah, that too.

39:30.447 --> 39:32.651
Hey, don't get involved.

39:32.651 --> 39:37.404
I'm a third party. This is between them.

39:45.312 --> 39:47.672
- Lim Seung Jun.
- What?

39:47.672 --> 39:48.840
Just tell me straight.

39:48.840 --> 39:52.976
Do you still like that girl from Soonmu Market?

39:52.976 --> 39:54.804
Why are you asking me that all of a sudden?

39:54.804 --> 39:57.493
Just answer me. Do you or not?

39:57.493 --> 39:59.090
I do.

39:59.090 --> 40:01.823
How do you just stop liking someone overnight?

40:01.823 --> 40:03.620
I'm not that kind of guy.

40:03.620 --> 40:07.365
Good. Hey, come here.

40:07.365 --> 40:10.284
[SLAMDUNK Full Original Set]
Is this it?

40:10.284 --> 40:14.151
Yeah. Our memories...

40:14.151 --> 40:15.935
I guess she's really trying to forget me.

40:15.935 --> 40:17.327
Get a grip!

40:17.327 --> 40:19.120
Why do you think she's trying to forget you?

40:19.120 --> 40:21.832
It means she hasn't moved on yet.

40:21.832 --> 40:23.411
Come on, just spend a little.

40:23.411 --> 40:24.792
[Chocolate Killer]
I'll take them.

40:24.792 --> 40:27.466
I'll take everything you listed,
including the comics.

40:27.466 --> 40:30.479
Can we meet in person?

40:31.969 --> 40:33.897
Wait, how did you even find this?

40:35.224 --> 40:36.488
Well...

40:36.488 --> 40:40.814
I'll tell you later if things work out, okay?

40:53.114 --> 40:56.493
She should be off by now...

40:57.873 --> 40:59.281
[Ui Yeong]

41:05.034 --> 41:08.658
Where are you? Why weren't you answering?

41:08.658 --> 41:10.682
I met up with Seung Jun after work.

41:10.682 --> 41:12.706
Oh, Seung Jun?

41:12.706 --> 41:14.733
Then...

41:14.733 --> 41:17.050
- What about me?
- Sorry?

41:17.050 --> 41:22.300
Didn't you miss me? I missed you.

41:25.115 --> 41:30.989
Say that again. I like how that sounds.

41:30.989 --> 41:33.286
I miss you, Ui Yeong.

41:33.286 --> 41:35.876
Come see me.

41:42.094 --> 41:46.663
- Looks like everyone's gone home.
- Yeah.

41:46.663 --> 41:50.983
Wow, so this is where you work.

41:50.983 --> 41:53.113
It's really nice.

41:53.113 --> 41:58.077
This is where we do paperwork,
design, meetings... all that.

41:58.077 --> 42:01.143
And this is my desk.

42:01.143 --> 42:04.369
Best spot in the place.

42:04.369 --> 42:07.860
Feels like you could really work freely here.

42:07.860 --> 42:09.884
Yeah, but in reality,

42:09.884 --> 42:13.309
sawdust gets everywhere,
so we have to air it out a lot.

42:13.309 --> 42:15.593
And this is the workshop.

42:15.593 --> 42:17.706
The workshop?

42:17.706 --> 42:18.935
Careful.

42:18.935 --> 42:22.929
We haven't cleaned up yet,
so you might get a splinter.

42:22.929 --> 42:26.242
Too dangerous. I'll just stay right here.

42:27.508 --> 42:34.629
- There's so much cool stuff here.
- This is a table saw for cutting.

42:34.629 --> 42:36.406
A table saw?

42:36.406 --> 42:39.210
- And this is a band saw.
- A band saw.

42:39.210 --> 42:42.600
This is a drill press. It's for drilling holes.

42:42.600 --> 42:44.184
A drill press...

42:44.184 --> 42:48.137
I have no idea what any of this is.

42:48.137 --> 42:50.780
Since you're here,
can you help me with something?

42:50.780 --> 42:53.406
With what?

43:07.115 --> 43:11.868
I need sample measurements
for a chair I'm submitting for the exhibition.

43:11.868 --> 43:16.306
I feel like you're getting to know me
a little too well.

43:16.306 --> 43:19.452
No, not even close.

43:21.146 --> 43:24.366
I want to know you more.

43:31.152 --> 43:34.776
Let's not stick to just weekends anymore.

43:34.776 --> 43:36.776
Let's just see each other whenever we want.

43:36.776 --> 43:39.823
I think I'd like that.

43:50.850 --> 43:54.377
Sir.

43:54.377 --> 43:57.330
Sir? Did he already leave?

43:57.330 --> 44:00.430
We brought late-night snacks.

44:02.386 --> 44:04.277
Guess we have no choice.

44:04.277 --> 44:07.747
If the boss isn't here,
we might as well have a beer.

44:07.747 --> 44:10.705
- Jin Su, run to the convenience store.
- Okay.

44:10.705 --> 44:12.019
You like beer, right?

44:12.019 --> 44:15.553
- Are we allowed to drink?
- Of course not.

44:15.553 --> 44:18.484
The boss says
we can do whatever we want in the office,

44:18.484 --> 44:19.986
except for two things.

44:19.986 --> 44:21.799
Drinking and dating.

44:21.799 --> 44:27.151
Because they're too exciting,
get your blood pumping...

44:27.151 --> 44:29.704
and make things dangerous.

44:31.383 --> 44:34.736
- Cheers.
- Cheers!

44:39.338 --> 44:42.492
- It's even better when you're sneaking it.
- This is the life.

44:42.492 --> 44:44.066
- Let's eat.
- Let's dig in.

44:44.066 --> 44:46.098
- My legs hurt.
- Your legs?

44:46.098 --> 44:48.617
Yeah, hold on.

44:51.404 --> 44:53.670
What was that?

44:53.670 --> 44:54.979
Hey, who's there!

44:54.979 --> 44:58.788
- What the hell?
- I said, who's there!

44:58.788 --> 45:00.578
Hey.

45:00.578 --> 45:03.922
Where are you going? Sae Byeok?

45:03.922 --> 45:06.336
What the...

45:12.789 --> 45:14.814
- Jin Su.
- Yeah?

45:14.814 --> 45:15.833
Go.

45:15.833 --> 45:17.754
Darn it.

45:17.754 --> 45:19.244
Come out right now!

45:19.244 --> 45:21.155
I'm calling the cops!

45:21.155 --> 45:23.668
We've got a weapon!

45:27.167 --> 45:29.357
Come out before I count to three.

45:29.357 --> 45:32.270
- One.
- Two.

45:32.270 --> 45:35.250
- Three!
- Three.

45:35.938 --> 45:38.642
- Hello.
- Why are you here, sir?

45:38.642 --> 45:42.428
My leg... Oh, hello.

45:42.428 --> 45:44.195
Ui Yeong?

45:44.195 --> 45:45.999
Oh, Sae Byeok.

45:45.999 --> 45:52.119
You're settling in really well here. I'm glad.

45:52.119 --> 45:56.149
Why are you two here together?

45:56.149 --> 45:57.929
Well...

45:57.929 --> 46:00.632
We're dating.

46:00.632 --> 46:03.742
You two?

46:03.742 --> 46:06.602
Sir, you can't be dating at the office.

46:06.602 --> 46:09.272
That's way too dangerous.

46:09.272 --> 46:14.256
You guys were drinking in here.
That's pretty dangerous too, isn't it?

46:14.256 --> 46:16.482
Right?

46:20.249 --> 46:22.754
Congrats.

46:45.089 --> 46:46.939
HeungJeongMangJeong?

46:46.939 --> 46:49.889
Chocolate Killer?

46:49.889 --> 46:52.608
Choco...

47:01.599 --> 47:02.852
Yeah, that's you.

47:02.852 --> 47:06.999
You don't even eat chocolate,
so what's with the name?

47:06.999 --> 47:10.390
And using someone else's account like this?

47:10.390 --> 47:13.567
That's grounds for a permanent ban, you know.

47:13.567 --> 47:15.411
No idea. Go ahead and report me.

47:15.411 --> 47:18.471
Honestly, every time I open that app,
I just think of you.

47:18.471 --> 47:22.291
I'll delete my account anyway.

47:22.291 --> 47:25.357
This'll be my last trade.

47:27.844 --> 47:31.404
It's 50,000 won.
Let's just finish this. Pay up.

47:32.864 --> 47:34.282
Not just like that.

47:34.282 --> 47:37.372
Let's make one more bet.
If you win, I'll give you 100,000 won.

47:37.372 --> 47:39.018
No, I'll give you 150,000 won.

47:39.018 --> 47:42.063
What is this, some kind of auction? Forget it.

47:42.063 --> 47:45.569
Then how high does it have to go?

47:46.694 --> 47:48.818
And if you win?

47:48.818 --> 47:52.324
You're clearly after something. Right?

47:54.825 --> 47:57.371
Just

47:57.371 --> 48:00.091
hear me out.

48:00.091 --> 48:02.891
That's all I want.

48:06.475 --> 48:08.499
I was too embarrassed to say this, but...

48:08.499 --> 48:10.440
I used to play basketball.

48:10.440 --> 48:15.121
I was training to go pro through college,
but I tore my ACL and had to quit.

48:15.121 --> 48:18.152
Since then, I think I've been holding back,
physically and emotionally.

48:18.152 --> 48:20.879
That's why I kept things light with you.

48:20.879 --> 48:25.312
A way to protect myself
from getting hurt first.

48:25.312 --> 48:27.483
I'm sorry.

48:27.483 --> 48:30.409
You said you'd talk after you win.

48:30.409 --> 48:33.447
Win first, then we talk. I'm not listening.

48:33.447 --> 48:36.036
Come on, let's go.

49:38.163 --> 49:40.848
[High Score]
[Player Score]

49:40.848 --> 49:43.068
They say the game ends

49:43.068 --> 49:45.983
the moment you give up.

49:52.729 --> 49:55.643
I really like you.

49:55.643 --> 49:58.489
I had to tell you that.

50:09.654 --> 50:11.498
Here we are.

50:11.498 --> 50:14.445
You must be tired after such a long trip.

50:14.445 --> 50:17.883
- I'm fine.
- Right this way.

50:17.883 --> 50:19.553
- Welcome.
- Hello.

50:19.553 --> 50:21.873
- He's here.
- Thanks for coming all this way.

50:21.873 --> 50:22.932
[High-value Chikso]

50:22.932 --> 50:24.531
[Lee Dae Livestock's differentiated strategy]
This is really impressive.

50:24.531 --> 50:25.616
I know, right?

50:25.616 --> 50:27.393
[Artificial Insemination Technician License]
As for our Chikso...

50:27.393 --> 50:32.225
We bring in one strong bull at a time
from breeders all across the country.

50:32.225 --> 50:36.237
I handle the breeding myself,
and raise them like my own sons.

50:36.237 --> 50:37.938
You've raised your Chikso with such care.

50:37.938 --> 50:40.688
We'll make sure they're treated
like the premium they are.

50:40.688 --> 50:44.568
Of course you should.

50:44.568 --> 50:46.732
But that young lady...

50:46.732 --> 50:50.143
Those bright, pretty eyes...

50:50.143 --> 50:53.837
they remind me of my cute Chikso.

50:53.837 --> 50:56.548
Your Chikso?

50:56.548 --> 50:57.904
She does. Totally.

50:57.904 --> 51:01.848
That's a new one.
But thank you, I appreciate it.

51:01.848 --> 51:04.765
By the way, my mouth's getting dry.

51:04.765 --> 51:08.141
Got anything to drink? Something sweet.

51:08.141 --> 51:10.688
I'll go grab some juice.

51:10.688 --> 51:12.481
We'll bring some cookies too.

51:12.481 --> 51:14.412
- Okay.
- We'll be right back.

51:14.412 --> 51:15.536
Thank you.

51:15.536 --> 51:18.431
We should've had that ready beforehand.

51:20.347 --> 51:22.371
He's not as stubborn as I expected.

51:22.371 --> 51:25.931
- Yeah.
- That's a relief.

51:25.931 --> 51:27.495
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

51:27.495 --> 51:31.811
I'm looking for a partner
I can trust for the long haul.

51:31.811 --> 51:33.381
That's exactly what we want too.

51:33.381 --> 51:35.254
This could be a great opportunity

51:35.254 --> 51:38.257
to build a long-term partnership with us.

51:38.257 --> 51:40.014
- But...
- Yes?

51:40.014 --> 51:44.032
That young lady earlier,
the one with the bright eyes.

51:44.032 --> 51:45.704
The bright eyes?

51:45.704 --> 51:47.057
Oh, yeah.

51:47.057 --> 51:51.559
Does she have a boyfriend?

51:51.559 --> 51:53.939
A boyfriend?

51:53.939 --> 51:57.109
- I do have a youngest son.
- Yeah.

51:57.109 --> 52:00.078
That boy of mine only lives for Chikso.

52:00.078 --> 52:01.743
He's got zero interest in dating.

52:01.743 --> 52:05.018
If young people like them spend time together,

52:05.018 --> 52:09.413
talk about work, talk about life...

52:09.413 --> 52:10.873
they might grow close.

52:10.873 --> 52:14.539
And what better partnership is there

52:14.539 --> 52:16.879
than something that strong and genuine?

52:16.879 --> 52:18.862
I see.

52:18.862 --> 52:22.415
So that's the kind of relationship
you're looking for.

52:29.552 --> 52:32.111
What do I do?

52:37.503 --> 52:40.910
That wrapped up way smoother than expected.

52:40.910 --> 52:43.655
Then I'll go ahead
and handle the contract details.

52:43.655 --> 52:46.953
No, no.

52:46.953 --> 52:50.039
Ms. Ui Yeong should take it.

52:51.404 --> 52:52.642
Sorry?

52:52.642 --> 52:56.488
But Mrs. Na Ri was the one
who found the vendor,

52:56.488 --> 52:59.245
and she handled the meeting
and all the research.

52:59.245 --> 53:01.382
I know.

53:01.382 --> 53:03.406
Ms. Ui Yeong, just go ahead and take it.

53:03.406 --> 53:06.970
There's a lot coming up anyway,
like managing the recipes.

53:06.970 --> 53:08.722
- And the chef trusts you.
- But...

53:08.722 --> 53:10.745
And you...

53:10.745 --> 53:13.229
- Thank you for your hard work.
- Sir!

53:13.229 --> 53:17.655
Man, why am I so tired these days?
Is it my liver or something?

53:26.509 --> 53:27.533
[A premium breed connecting tradition
and the future Chikso]

53:27.533 --> 53:31.483
So I think I'll have to go to a meeting
after work tomorrow.

53:31.483 --> 53:32.708
But

53:32.708 --> 53:35.207
Mrs. Na Ri won't hand over
any of the materials.

53:35.207 --> 53:37.587
Sounds like she's pretty upset.

53:37.587 --> 53:40.807
Redoing all that research in a day
won't be easy.

53:40.807 --> 53:41.880
Still...

53:41.880 --> 53:44.901
Talking to you actually makes me feel better.

53:44.901 --> 53:48.789
Nothing's really changed, but... yeah.

53:48.789 --> 53:51.223
You can talk to me anytime.

53:51.223 --> 53:53.483
Want me to pick you up after?

53:53.483 --> 53:54.928
Oh, no.

53:54.928 --> 53:56.672
I don't even know when it'll end.

53:56.672 --> 53:58.605
Let's just meet this weekend.

53:58.605 --> 54:00.301
Are you working late again tonight?

54:00.301 --> 54:03.673
Yeah, but I split the work with the team,
so it's manageable.

54:03.673 --> 54:07.157
I'll call you when I get home.

54:07.157 --> 54:09.143
Bye.

54:15.586 --> 54:17.882
[HANKUK UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL]

54:17.882 --> 54:21.572
[HKUH Hospital Director Inauguration
and Retirement Ceremony]

54:21.572 --> 54:23.442
Sir,

54:23.442 --> 54:25.118
congratulations.

54:25.118 --> 54:26.918
Thank you.

54:26.918 --> 54:30.805
- It's an honor.
- My pleasure. Thank you.

54:35.506 --> 54:38.265
I'm kind of excited.

54:38.265 --> 54:41.296
I finally get to introduce you as my wife.

54:41.296 --> 54:43.233
I'm not the supportive-wife type.

54:43.233 --> 54:45.593
I'm just here to congratulate you.

54:45.593 --> 54:47.617
I know.

54:47.617 --> 54:49.997
- That's actually why I invited you.
- What?

54:49.997 --> 54:53.327
I saw you at the awards ceremony.

54:53.327 --> 54:57.444
You're really good at clapping.

54:57.444 --> 55:01.028
Next, we will present a plaque of appreciation
to our new hospital director, Shin Ji Hoon,

55:01.028 --> 55:04.894
and invite him to give his inaugural remarks.

55:14.377 --> 55:16.401
Distinguished faculty and staff,

55:16.401 --> 55:19.406
I take the responsibility of serving as

55:19.406 --> 55:21.230
Director of HKUH very seriously.

55:21.230 --> 55:24.790
I will devote myself to ensuring
that our hospital continues to lead

55:24.790 --> 55:26.068
the future of medicine.

55:26.068 --> 55:28.654
The values and trust our hospital holds today

55:28.654 --> 55:33.954
have been built by all of you here.

55:33.954 --> 55:38.105
I'll do everything I can to carry those values

55:38.105 --> 55:41.019
and that trust forward.

55:41.019 --> 55:43.438
Thank you.

55:51.673 --> 55:54.102
One, two, three.

55:54.102 --> 55:55.512
One more time.

55:55.512 --> 55:58.172
One, two, three.

55:59.446 --> 56:00.644
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

56:00.644 --> 56:03.108
Thank you.

56:05.518 --> 56:08.902
- The camera doesn't do you justice.
- Hello.

56:08.902 --> 56:11.863
I heard you two met as doctor and patient,

56:11.863 --> 56:13.740
and even spent time together in Cannes.

56:13.740 --> 56:16.021
We just happened to run into each other.

56:16.021 --> 56:17.571
We're doctors too,

56:17.571 --> 56:19.991
how come we never get that kind of fate?

56:19.991 --> 56:21.728
He's just a doctor like the rest of you.

56:21.728 --> 56:25.359
So you must've gotten close back then,
in Cannes?

56:25.359 --> 56:27.941
Kind of.

56:27.941 --> 56:29.286
I hope to see you all more often.

56:29.286 --> 56:31.726
Please take good care of Dr. Shin.

56:31.726 --> 56:34.472
Thank you.

56:38.940 --> 56:41.143
So they didn't meet at the hospital...

56:41.143 --> 56:43.070
but it still counts as an affair.

56:43.070 --> 56:46.674
And his wife was critically ill at the time.
That's what makes it worse.

56:46.674 --> 56:48.752
Everyone knows he was in France,

56:48.752 --> 56:52.415
ignoring calls from his son and the hospital.

56:52.415 --> 56:54.635
Right.

56:55.428 --> 56:57.256
That's just too much.

56:57.256 --> 57:00.711
You really can't trust anyone these days, huh?

57:32.194 --> 57:33.572
Hello.

57:33.572 --> 57:35.169
Ms. Ui Yeong.

57:35.169 --> 57:37.242
- Oh, hello.
- Yeah.

57:37.242 --> 57:40.659
You're looking really good today.

57:40.659 --> 57:42.816
Really? Thank you.

57:42.816 --> 57:47.620
So, you've been going on
a lot of blind dates lately, right?

57:47.620 --> 57:49.564
- Yes.
- Well, you know how it is.

57:49.564 --> 57:51.690
Even if nothing comes of it,

57:51.690 --> 57:53.907
it's all experience.

57:53.907 --> 57:56.740
And if one works out, that's a jackpot.

57:56.740 --> 57:59.745
- I guess that's true.
- Anyway, about the meeting...

57:59.745 --> 58:01.700
I booked Herod in Cheongdam.

58:01.700 --> 58:03.077
Here, take this.

58:03.077 --> 58:07.757
Go enjoy something nice, alright?

58:07.757 --> 58:10.401
It's the owner's youngest son, right?

58:10.401 --> 58:12.279
The one in charge of Chikso meat.

58:12.279 --> 58:15.016
Given the owner's age,
he's probably around your age.

58:15.016 --> 58:18.680
But it's a big ranch,
tons of expensive cattle...

58:18.680 --> 58:21.613
so basically, mid-sized business family.

58:21.613 --> 58:24.450
Medium. Like steak.

58:24.450 --> 58:28.541
- Good luck.
- Yeah.

58:28.541 --> 58:31.361
Medium steak?

58:40.236 --> 58:42.335
Mrs. Na Ri.

58:44.029 --> 58:46.019
What is it?

58:46.019 --> 58:49.716
About today's meeting materials.

58:49.716 --> 58:52.512
Since you put so much work into them,

58:52.512 --> 58:54.146
I'll make sure

58:54.146 --> 58:59.172
I do my best and not let you down.

59:01.921 --> 59:04.181
Okay.

59:17.320 --> 59:18.750
Sir,

59:18.750 --> 59:23.970
could we meet at the cafe
in front of the hotel?

59:27.670 --> 59:30.543
- Here you go.
- Thanks.

59:33.918 --> 59:38.217
So, what did you want to talk about?

59:41.901 --> 59:44.753
That's kind of disappointing, sir.

59:44.753 --> 59:47.384
I know Ms. Ui Yeong's good at her job.
She motivates me too.

59:47.384 --> 59:50.371
But not this time.

59:50.371 --> 59:53.236
You know I've been working late for days.

59:53.236 --> 59:56.108
Of course I know. Everyone does.

59:56.108 --> 59:57.792
I know how hard you've worked.

59:57.792 --> 59:59.951
Then why are you doing this?

59:59.951 --> 01:00:02.295
I can handle it.

01:00:02.295 --> 01:00:05.926
- I can still go to the meeting...
- Come on!

01:00:05.926 --> 01:00:08.766
I said no. Don't push it.

01:00:08.766 --> 01:00:11.727
If you don't want this to blow up,

01:00:11.727 --> 01:00:14.133
- just sit this one out.
- Why?

01:00:14.133 --> 01:00:16.250
Then give me a reason!

01:00:16.250 --> 01:00:19.933
You have children and...

01:00:19.933 --> 01:00:21.803
a husband.

01:00:21.803 --> 01:00:24.416
Whatever. I'm off.

01:00:24.416 --> 01:00:27.229
- I don't know.
- Sir!

01:00:35.249 --> 01:00:38.355
The more I think about it, the angrier I get.

01:00:38.355 --> 01:00:40.853
Yeah, I've skipped a few site visits before,

01:00:40.853 --> 01:00:43.406
using my husband or in-laws as an excuse.

01:00:43.406 --> 01:00:47.413
But I've earned that by now, haven't I?

01:00:47.413 --> 01:00:48.950
That doesn't mean

01:00:48.950 --> 01:00:52.263
you just cut me out of the work.

01:00:52.263 --> 01:00:54.366
"Because you have a husband, you can't do it."

01:00:54.366 --> 01:00:57.472
Does that even make sense?

01:00:58.867 --> 01:01:01.370
Pushing out someone who wants to work...

01:01:01.370 --> 01:01:03.171
That's just not right.

01:01:03.171 --> 01:01:06.177
When is the meeting?

01:01:06.991 --> 01:01:09.115
She probably just left.

01:01:09.115 --> 01:01:11.388
Some place in Cheongdam... Herod?

01:01:11.388 --> 01:01:14.155
That's what I heard.

01:01:14.155 --> 01:01:15.945
People have meetings at places like that?

01:01:15.945 --> 01:01:17.585
Why? You know it?

01:01:17.585 --> 01:01:20.351
Yeah, I used to work there.

01:01:20.351 --> 01:01:23.729
But for a meeting, the vibe's a bit off.

01:01:23.729 --> 01:01:27.622
It's actually a pretty famous blind date spot.

01:01:28.769 --> 01:01:31.516
Wait.

01:01:31.516 --> 01:01:36.589
He said the son handling operations
would be there today.

01:01:38.782 --> 01:01:43.799
So the reason I can't go is...

01:01:43.799 --> 01:01:46.479
- A blind date?
- A blind date?

01:01:51.765 --> 01:01:54.355
Excuse me, are you Ms. Lee Ui Yeong?

01:01:54.355 --> 01:01:55.512
[Mrs. Na Ri]

01:01:55.512 --> 01:01:56.965
Are you Mr. Choi's youngest son?

01:01:56.965 --> 01:01:59.369
- Yeah, right.
- Hello.

01:01:59.369 --> 01:02:01.674
I'm Lee Ui Yeong
from The Hills purchasing team.

01:02:01.674 --> 01:02:04.071
Oh, your card?

01:02:04.071 --> 01:02:06.755
Here's mine.

01:02:06.755 --> 01:02:09.005
- I'm Choi Woo Jun.
- Yeah.

01:02:09.005 --> 01:02:12.972
The traffic on the way here was no joke.

01:02:12.972 --> 01:02:15.302
You must've come from pretty far.

01:02:15.302 --> 01:02:16.823
Never mind.

01:02:16.823 --> 01:02:18.352
Shall we head in?

01:02:18.352 --> 01:02:20.588
- Yes.
- Yeah.

01:02:23.738 --> 01:02:27.005
This looks amazing. I'm so starving.

01:02:27.005 --> 01:02:29.030
Would you like to order a full meal?

01:02:29.030 --> 01:02:30.694
Yes, of course.

01:02:30.694 --> 01:02:33.047
Alright.

01:02:34.124 --> 01:02:36.627
This is a bit tricky.

01:02:36.627 --> 01:02:40.297
I'll just go with meat.
You can pick something good.

01:02:40.297 --> 01:02:42.836
Oh, okay.

01:02:44.044 --> 01:02:46.423
Excuse me.

01:02:48.567 --> 01:02:52.090
We'll have two steaks, please.

01:02:52.090 --> 01:02:54.414
Okay, how would you like them cooked?

01:02:54.414 --> 01:02:55.678
Oh, for that...

01:02:55.678 --> 01:02:59.547
If it's fresh, go medium rare.
Otherwise, medium.

01:02:59.547 --> 01:03:00.908
Would you like some wine?

01:03:00.908 --> 01:03:02.971
We'll take two glasses of wine.

01:03:02.971 --> 01:03:05.435
Sure, I'll bring that right out.

01:03:05.435 --> 01:03:07.757
Thank you.

01:03:12.499 --> 01:03:13.847
The person you're calling is...

01:03:13.847 --> 01:03:17.767
Neither the team manager
nor Ui Yeong is picking up.

01:03:22.631 --> 01:03:24.690
Hello?

01:03:25.390 --> 01:03:27.135
Oh, honey.

01:03:27.135 --> 01:03:29.180
Did you get off work?

01:03:29.180 --> 01:03:32.827
Yeah, I'm heading out too. Okay.

01:03:33.493 --> 01:03:36.150
What should I do?
I think I need to head out first.

01:03:36.150 --> 01:03:38.540
I'll keep trying to reach her once I get home.

01:03:38.540 --> 01:03:42.064
- One of them will pick up eventually, huh?
- Yeah.

01:03:42.064 --> 01:03:44.872
- Hello.
- Good afternoon.

01:03:44.872 --> 01:03:46.024
Is everything okay?

01:03:46.024 --> 01:03:49.594
Sir, something came up.
I need to leave a little early today.

01:03:49.594 --> 01:03:51.812
- Okay.
- Thank you.

01:03:51.812 --> 01:03:53.932
Yeah.

01:04:00.583 --> 01:04:02.608
My dad said

01:04:02.608 --> 01:04:06.841
your eyes look just like our calves.

01:04:06.841 --> 01:04:09.008
He was right.

01:04:09.008 --> 01:04:12.332
At the market, calves with eyes like that

01:04:12.332 --> 01:04:14.763
get snapped up fast.

01:04:14.763 --> 01:04:19.021
It's surprising... you're still single.

01:04:19.769 --> 01:04:21.742
Yeah.

01:04:23.977 --> 01:04:27.761
This is our hotel proposal.

01:04:27.761 --> 01:04:30.547
Oh, okay.

01:04:31.571 --> 01:04:33.022
[Ark of Flavor Selection]

01:04:33.022 --> 01:04:34.254
This is just a draft.

01:04:34.254 --> 01:04:38.600
You can adjust the items and quantities
to fit Lee Dae Livestock.

01:04:41.241 --> 01:04:42.392
Oh, the food's here.

01:04:42.392 --> 01:04:45.884
- Why don't we eat first?
- Sure.

01:04:45.884 --> 01:04:47.668
Thank you.

01:04:47.668 --> 01:04:50.168
This looks great.

01:04:54.997 --> 01:04:56.941
It's practically raw.

01:04:56.941 --> 01:04:58.598
You're lucky you met me today.

01:04:58.598 --> 01:05:02.606
Didn't know I'm great with a knife, huh?

01:05:04.050 --> 01:05:07.229
Guess I'll have to show her.

01:05:09.298 --> 01:05:11.406
- Excuse me...
- Yeah?

01:05:11.406 --> 01:05:14.692
You should use this knife.

01:05:20.360 --> 01:05:24.981
Next to someone like you,
I must look like a total country bumpkin, huh?

01:05:24.981 --> 01:05:26.547
No, not at all.

01:05:26.547 --> 01:05:31.131
At home, I just use scissors
and cut my meat however I like.

01:05:31.131 --> 01:05:34.509
You're more down-to-earth than you look.

01:05:34.509 --> 01:05:37.616
It's really nice meeting you like this.

01:05:46.911 --> 01:05:49.636
Another glass of wine, please.

01:05:49.636 --> 01:05:54.595
Hey, fill it up. Don't hold back.

01:05:58.908 --> 01:06:01.373
This is good.

01:06:10.096 --> 01:06:12.429
Over here!

01:06:16.418 --> 01:06:20.404
Man, I'm getting all fired up.

01:06:37.569 --> 01:06:41.900
If we keep drinking,
we won't get any work done,

01:06:41.900 --> 01:06:45.546
- and we might not even make it home.
- You know...

01:06:45.546 --> 01:06:47.874
I'll move a little closer.

01:06:47.874 --> 01:06:51.127
Guys in this line of work,

01:06:51.127 --> 01:06:55.606
we mess around, do arm wrestling and stuff.

01:06:55.606 --> 01:06:58.690
Our forearms get so built,
we can barely control them.

01:06:58.690 --> 01:07:00.560
- Here, feel this.
- Sorry?

01:07:00.560 --> 01:07:03.074
- No, I'm okay.
- You can relax around me.

01:07:03.074 --> 01:07:06.921
I can see it just fine.

01:07:06.921 --> 01:07:08.271
Don't play innocent.

01:07:08.271 --> 01:07:10.839
You haven't dated much, have you?

01:07:10.839 --> 01:07:12.922
You're old enough to know how this works.

01:07:12.922 --> 01:07:14.908
When you keep acting like
you don't know anything,

01:07:14.908 --> 01:07:17.949
it kills the mood.

01:07:17.949 --> 01:07:20.829
So how many guys have you dated?

01:07:20.829 --> 01:07:24.062
Three? Four?

01:07:24.708 --> 01:07:27.811
What a piece of work.

01:07:27.811 --> 01:07:29.942
Sorry, sir.

01:07:29.942 --> 01:07:31.527
Yeah?

01:07:31.527 --> 01:07:34.904
You know, we're in a meeting right now.

01:07:34.904 --> 01:07:39.443
Please keep your questions related to business.

01:07:42.108 --> 01:07:45.606
All you've been doing is talking business.

01:07:45.606 --> 01:07:49.159
You should be more accommodating with me.

01:07:49.159 --> 01:07:53.123
That is how things go smoothly,
including the work.

01:07:53.123 --> 01:07:56.221
So you have been trying to impress me. Right?

01:07:56.221 --> 01:07:58.853
Ms. Ui Yeong, am I wrong?

01:07:58.853 --> 01:08:00.090
To be clear,

01:08:00.090 --> 01:08:03.403
I'm being polite because I want to show

01:08:03.403 --> 01:08:06.558
trust and respect as a business partner.

01:08:06.558 --> 01:08:10.011
I have no intention of
gaining your personal interest.

01:08:10.011 --> 01:08:11.875
- What?
- So I would appreciate it

01:08:11.875 --> 01:08:16.201
if you focused on whether our proposal
benefits your company.

01:08:16.201 --> 01:08:18.058
Not on me.

01:08:18.058 --> 01:08:19.388
Please review the proposal.

01:08:19.388 --> 01:08:21.577
I'll step out and make a quick call
to my office.

01:08:21.577 --> 01:08:24.123
Hold on.

01:08:27.163 --> 01:08:29.426
Are you just going to ignore me?

01:08:29.426 --> 01:08:30.713
Sit down.

01:08:30.713 --> 01:08:33.686
I said sit down!

01:08:37.326 --> 01:08:40.302
I think you've had too much to drink.

01:08:40.302 --> 01:08:43.077
Let's wrap up the meeting here.

01:08:43.077 --> 01:08:46.326
I'll follow up later.

01:08:46.326 --> 01:08:47.997
Hey, where are you going?

01:08:47.997 --> 01:08:49.617
That hurts. Let go!

01:08:49.617 --> 01:08:51.985
- You're just going to walk away like that?
- Please let go of my hand!

01:08:51.985 --> 01:08:54.371
- That hurts!
- Hey!

01:08:58.840 --> 01:09:00.398
Tae Seop?

01:09:00.398 --> 01:09:01.851
Who the hell are you?

01:09:01.851 --> 01:09:04.274
Me? Her boyfriend.

01:09:04.274 --> 01:09:05.964
What?

01:09:33.456 --> 01:09:37.108
[Congrats on officially
being in a relationship]

01:09:48.601 --> 01:09:52.725
[I really like you]

01:09:52.725 --> 01:09:56.086
[That's way too dangerous]

01:10:00.980 --> 01:10:04.854
How did you know to come?

01:10:04.854 --> 01:10:08.924
While the disciplinary committee
wraps up for the team manager...

01:10:08.924 --> 01:10:10.427
I've got nothing to do.

01:10:10.427 --> 01:10:12.867
All that stuff you've been putting off...

01:10:12.867 --> 01:10:15.380
Start with that.

01:10:15.380 --> 01:10:17.057
This is for you.

01:10:17.057 --> 01:10:19.887
I'm getting a divorce.

01:10:19.887 --> 01:10:21.001
What?

01:10:21.001 --> 01:10:23.224
Your time off's almost over.

01:10:23.224 --> 01:10:26.917
How about a quick trip together?

01:10:29.078 --> 01:10:32.505
- Dad?
- Your dad?
